{"book":10,"chapter":7,"context":{"chapter":7,"title":"God Promises David a House","summary":"David wants to build a house for the ark, but God says no: instead God will build David a 'house,' a dynasty. David's son will build the temple, and David's throne will be established forever. David responds with a humble prayer of thanks.","background":"The chapter plays on the word 'house': palace, temple and royal family. This promise, often called the Davidic covenant, became the root of Israel's hope for a coming king from David's line (Psalm 89; Isaiah 9:7). The New Testament applies verse 14, 'I will be his father, and he shall be my son,' to Jesus (Hebrews 1:5).","customs":[{"term":"House of cedar","verses":"7:2","note":"Cedar from Lebanon was costly, fragrant and durable. David contrasts his palace with the tent that housed the ark."}],"watchFor":["'House' shifts meaning through the chapter (vv. 2, 5, 11, 13, 16).","'Who am I, O Lord God?' (v. 18).","'For ever' echoes through God's promise and David's prayer (vv. 13, 16, 24–29)."],"connections":["1 Chronicles 17:1-15","Psalms 89:3-4","Luke 1:32-33","Hebrews 1:5"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it was"],["כִּי","ki-","H3588","HTc","that"],["יָשַׁב","yashav","H3427","HVqp3ms","he dwelt"],["הַמֶּלֶךְ","hamelekh","H4428","HTd/Ncmsa","the king"],["בְּבֵיתוֹ","beveito","H1004","HR/Ncmsc/Sp3ms","in house his"],["וַיהוָה","vayahweh","H3068","HC/Npt","and Yahweh"],["הֵנִיחַ","heniach-","H5117","HVhp3ms","he had given rest"],["לוֹ","lo","H9033","HRd/Sp3ms","to <the> him"],["מִסָּבִיב","misaviv","H5439","HR/Ncbsa","from round about"],["מִכָּל","mikol","H3605","HR/Ncmsc","from all"],["אֹיְבָיו","'oyevav","H341","HVqrmpc/Sp3ms","enemies his"]],"x":[[20016007,20016007,7],[42001074,42001075,6],[11005004,11005004,5],[14014006,14014006,5],[6023001,6023001,4],[13017001,13017027,4],[19018001,19018001,4],[27004029,27004030,4]],"xn":8},"2":{"w":[["וַיֹּאמֶר","vaiyomer","H559","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he said"]